{"content":[{"c":["JESHUA (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Levite and head of the ninth of 24 divisions of priests formed during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.11","r":"1Chr.24.11","rawR":"1Chr.24.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.11","value":"1Chr.24.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 24:11"},"). He was perhaps the forefather of 973 descendants who returned with Zerubbabel to Judah following the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.36","r":"Ezra.2.36","rawR":"Ezra.2.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.36","value":"Ezra.2.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:36"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.39","r":"Neh.7.39","rawR":"Neh.7.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.39","value":"Neh.7.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:39"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of the Levites assisting Kore in the distribution of the offerings among his fellow priests living in the priestly cities of Judah during the days of King Hezekiah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.31.15","r":"2Chr.31.15","rawR":"2Chr.31.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.31.15","value":"2Chr.31.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 31:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Son of Jozadak (alternately “Jehozadak”) the high priest. Jozadak was deported by Nebuchadnezzar to Babylon (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.14-15","r":"1Chr.6.14-15","rawR":"1Chr.6.14-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.14-15","value":"1Chr.6.14-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:14-15"},"). Jeshua, Jozadak’s successor as high priest, returned with Zerubbabel to Jerusalem after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.2","r":"Ezra.2.2","rawR":"Ezra.2.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.2","value":"Ezra.2.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.7","r":"Neh.7.7","rawR":"Neh.7.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.7","value":"Neh.7.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.1","r":"Neh.12.1","rawR":"Neh.12.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.1","value":"Neh.12.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:1"},"). Upon arrival, he led his fellow priests in making the altar of God (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.3.2","r":"Ezra.3.2","rawR":"Ezra.3.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.3.2","value":"Ezra.3.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 3:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.5.2","r":"Ezra.5.2","rawR":"Ezra.5.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.5.2","value":"Ezra.5.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:2"},") and eventually headed up a construction program to rebuild the temple (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.3.8","r":"Ezra.3.8","rawR":"Ezra.3.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.3.8","value":"Ezra.3.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:8"},"). Confirmed as God’s leader by Haggai and Zechariah (",{"href":"?bref=Hagg.1.1-14","r":"Hagg.1.1-14","rawR":"Hagg.1.1-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hagg.1.1-14","value":"Hagg.1.1-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hg 1:1-14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Hagg.2.2,4","r":"Hagg.2.2,4","rawR":"Hagg.2.2,4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hagg.2.2,4","value":"Hagg.2.2,4"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:2, 4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Zech.3.1-9","r":"Zech.3.1-9","rawR":"Zech.3.1-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.3.1-9","value":"Zech.3.1-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zec 3:1-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Zech.6.11","r":"Zech.6.11","rawR":"Zech.6.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.6.11","value":"Zech.6.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:11"},"), Jeshua (alternately “Joshua” in these passages) resolutely resisted attempts by adversaries to infiltrate his people and hinder the work on the temple (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.4.3","r":"Ezra.4.3","rawR":"Ezra.4.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.4.3","value":"Ezra.4.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 4:3"},"). Joiakim was Jeshua’s son and successor as high priest, serving in the days of Nehemiah and Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.12,26","r":"Neh.12.12,26","rawR":"Neh.12.12,26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.12,26","value":"Neh.12.12,26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:12, 26"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Descendant of Pahath-moab and the forefather of a family of Jews who returned with Zerubbabel to Judah following the Babylonian captivity (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.6","r":"Ezra.2.6","rawR":"Ezra.2.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.6","value":"Ezra.2.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.11","r":"Neh.7.11","rawR":"Neh.7.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.11","value":"Neh.7.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Father of a family of Levites who returned to Jerusalem with Zerubbabel (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.40","r":"Ezra.2.40","rawR":"Ezra.2.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.40","value":"Ezra.2.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:40"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.43","r":"Neh.7.43","rawR":"Neh.7.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.43","value":"Neh.7.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:43"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.8","r":"Neh.12.8","rawR":"Neh.12.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.8","value":"Neh.12.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:8"},"). He and his sons were responsible for overseeing the workmen building the temple (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.3.9","r":"Ezra.3.9","rawR":"Ezra.3.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.3.9","value":"Ezra.3.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 3:9"},"; this Jeshua may be identical with #3 above)."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Levite and Jozabad’s father. Jozabad assisted Meremoth, Eleazar, and Noadiah with taking inventory of the temple’s precious metals and vessels during the days of Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.33","r":"Ezra.8.33","rawR":"Ezra.8.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.33","value":"Ezra.8.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:33"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. Ezer’s father. Ezer was ruler of Mizpah, who repaired a section of the Jerusalem wall during the days of Nehemiah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.19","r":"Neh.3.19","rawR":"Neh.3.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.19","value":"Neh.3.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:19"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["8. Azaniah’s son and a leader of the Levites in the days of Ezra and Nehemiah. Jeshua assisted Ezra with teaching the people the law (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.8.7","r":"Neh.8.7","rawR":"Neh.8.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.8.7","value":"Neh.8.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 8:7"},") and later set his seal on Ezra’s covenant (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.9","r":"Neh.10.9","rawR":"Neh.10.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.9","value":"Neh.10.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["9. Alternate spelling of Joshua, the son of Nun, in ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.8.17","r":"Neh.8.17","rawR":"Neh.8.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.8.17","value":"Neh.8.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 8:17"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=JoshuaPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JoshuaPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JoshuaPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Joshua (Person) #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"JeshuaPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 24:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.24.11","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.24.11","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.24.11"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 2:36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.2.36","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.2.36","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.2.36"},{"anchorText":"Neh 7:39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.7.39","rawQueryValue":"Neh.7.39","sourceRefExact":"Neh.7.39"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 31:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.31.15","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.31.15","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.31.15"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:14-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.14-15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.14-15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.14-15"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 2:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.2.2","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.2.2","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.2.2"},{"anchorText":"Neh 7:7","canonicaliz